{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int K = 33;\nconst long long mod = 1000000007;\n\nstruct matrix {\n    long long a[K][K];\n} t[K], ans, pre[K], suf[K];\nlong long n;\nint k;\n\nvoid multi(const matrix& m1, const matrix& m2, matrix& to) {\n    matrix tmp = {};\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j) {\n            long long sum = 0;\n            for (int p = 0; p <= k; ++p)\n                sum = (sum + m1.a[i][p] * m2.a[p][j]) % mod;\n            tmp.a[i][j] = sum;\n        }\n    to = tmp;\n}\n\nvoid init() {\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j)\n            ans.a[i][j] = (i == j) ? 1 : 0;\n    for (int p = 0; p < k; ++p)\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i)\n            for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j)\n                t[p].a[i][j] = (i == j || i == p) ? 1 : 0;\n}\n\nvoid work() {\n    vector<int> bit;\n    long long m = n;\n    while (m > 0) {\n        bit.push_back(m % k);\n        m /= k;\n    }\n    bit.push_back(0);\n    // manual partial sum from right\n    for (int i = bit.size() - 2; i >= 0; --i)\n        bit[i] += bit[i+1];\n\n    for (size_t p = 0; p < bit.size() - 1; ++p) {\n        for (int i = bit[p] - 1; i >= bit[p+1]; --i)\n            multi(t[i % k], ans, ans);\n\n        pre[0] = t[0];\n        for (int i = 1; i < k; ++i)\n            multi(pre[i-1], t[i], pre[i]);\n\n        suf[k-1] = t[k-1];\n        for (int i = k-2; i >= 0; --i)\n            multi(t[i], suf[i+1], suf[i]);\n\n        t[0] = suf[0];\n        for (int i = 1; i < k; ++i)\n            multi(suf[i], pre[i-1], t[i]);\n    }\n\n    long long sum = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i)\n        sum = (sum + ans.a[i][k]) % mod;\n    cout << sum << endl;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    init();\n    work();\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nK = 33\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef multi(m1, m2):\n    \"\"\"return m1 * m2 (mod MOD)\"\"\"\n    k = len(m1) - 1  # size is k+1\n    tmp = [[0] * (k+1) for _ in range(k+1)]\n    for i in range(k+1):\n        for j in range(k+1):\n            s = 0\n            for p in range(k+1):\n                s = (s + m1[i][p] * m2[p][j]) % MOD\n            tmp[i][j] = s\n    return tmp\n\ndef init():\n    global n, k, ans, t\n    n, k = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    # ans = identity matrix of size k+1\n    ans = [[0] * (k+1) for _ in range(k+1)]\n    for i in range(k+1):\n        ans[i][i] = 1\n    # t[p] for p in 0..k-1\n    t = []\n    for p in range(k):\n        mat = [[0] * (k+1) for _ in range(k+1)]\n        for i in range(k+1):\n            for j in range(k+1):\n                if i == j or i == p:\n                    mat[i][j] = 1\n                else:\n                    mat[i][j] = 0\n        t.append(mat)\n\ndef work():\n    global ans, t\n    # build base-k digits of n (least significant first)\n    bit = []\n    m = n\n    while m > 0:\n        bit.append(m % k)\n        m //= k\n    bit.append(0)  # extra zero at the end\n    # partial sum from right\n    for i in range(len(bit)-2, -1, -1):\n        bit[i] += bit[i+1]\n\n    for p in range(len(bit)-1):\n        # multiply ans by t[i%k] for i from bit[p]-1 down to bit[p+1]\n        for i in range(bit[p]-1, bit[p+1]-1, -1):\n            ans = multi(t[i % k], ans)\n\n        # pre[0] = t[0]; pre[i] = pre[i-1] * t[i]\n        pre = [None] * k\n        pre[0] = t[0]\n        for i in range(1, k):\n            pre[i] = multi(pre[i-1], t[i])\n\n        # suf[k-1] = t[k-1]; suf[i] = t[i] * suf[i+1]\n        suf = [None] * k\n        suf[k-1] = t[k-1]\n        for i in range(k-2, -1, -1):\n            suf[i] = multi(t[i], suf[i+1])\n\n        # update t: t[0] = suf[0]; for i=1..k-1: t[i] = suf[i] * pre[i-1]\n        t[0] = suf[0]\n        for i in range(1, k):\n            t[i] = multi(suf[i], pre[i-1])\n\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(k+1):\n        total = (total + ans[i][k]) % MOD\n    print(total)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    init()\n    work()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.764281842042692e-05, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00036399890086613595, -0.41714707016944885, -4.172316494077677e-06, -0.001177690108306706, -0.3288798928260803, -2.1576648578047752e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.015949550899677e-05, -0.0009662011871114373, -0.3868740200996399, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.1616290875244886e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.932505594799295e-05, -0.02330787293612957, -0.29324406385421753, -1.3589766240329482e-05, 0.0, -2.753696753643453e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.2523643672466278, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.5869265794754028, -1.1324206590652466, -0.0968947559595108, -9.715084888739511e-05, -0.0005989664932712913, 0.0, 0.0, -0.7311532497406006, -0.7542534470558167, -0.0017717868322506547, -0.08073355257511139, -0.